# Copy this file to input.txt and put what you want tagged in it.
# Lines starting with # are ignored, and so are blank lines.
#
# The file holds ONE of these two kinds of lines. The tagger works out
# which one you used (or set "mode: tags" / "mode: hashes" in config.yaml).
#
# 1) Hydrus search tags, one per line. A file must match all of them,
#    just like a search page in Hydrus. For example:
#
#      system:filetype is image
#      system:limit is 500
#      -wd v1.4 vit tagger v2 ai generated tags
#
# 2) File hashes (sha256), one per line. In Hydrus: select files, then
#    right-click > share > copy > hashes > sha256. For example:
#
#      0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef
#
# Remove the # in front of the line below (or replace it with your own).
# system:filetype is image
